abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of Shamir's theorem using Complexitylib's unchanged
  definitions of IP and PSPACE. The hard inclusion combines a uniform
  polynomial-time machine-to-QBF reduction, a certified algebraic interactive
  verifier, and closure of IP under polynomial-time reductions. The reverse
  inclusion is imported from Complexitylib. Developed with Codex assistance;
  original attribution is preserved for all vendored sources. This component
  is included in the TCS formalizations repository.
keywords:
  - computational complexity
  - interactive proofs
  - formal verification
  - Lean
  - PSPACE
